    "body": "I'm a little concerned by the amount of added configuration options something like this adds.\r\n\r\nIdeally, we would have `success_style`, `error_style`, `symbol` and `root_symbol`; similarly to how we have `style`, `not_capable_style`, and `symbol` for the Node.js module. The trade-off there being that folks wouldn't be able to change the error symbol. 🤔\r\n\r\nI'd be curious to hear the thoughts of other @starship/astronauts about how we could go about handling these cases.",
