    "body": "macOS's root user is disabled by default, `sudo` gives your **current user** root privileges, so this doesn't make much sense on macs.\n\nQuoting [Apple](https://support.apple.com/guide/directory-utility/about-the-root-user-dirub32398f1/mac):\n\n> The root user is disabled by default. Although you can enable it, it’s recommended that you avoid logging into a Mac as the root user, either locally or remotely.",
